    "body": "By LoadstarEditorial\n15 November 2026\nhttps://youtu.be/Xsa-surXQKE\nThis week on The Loadstar Podcast , we unpack the latest developments in US tariffs and customs enforcement, including tougher rules for foreign importers of record and what a Democrat-controlled Congress could mean for President Trump’s trade agenda.\nCargoTrans co-CEO Nunzio De Filippis joins us to explain the implications for importers, while The Loadstar ‘s Alex Lennane discusses the ‘dire’ situation facing European hauliers, why supply chain disruption is forcing shippers into costly emergency airfreight, and the impact of cargo bottlenecks at Bangkok and Shenzhen airports.\nPlus, we look at fresh challenges for the perishables sector, Freightos’ new AI platform and the growing tensions between its board and founder, Zvi Schreiber.\nClick here to receive an email notification every time we release a podcast.\nThis article is © The Loadstar. Reproduction, rewriting, or derivative use requires a license. Contact [email protected] for licensing enquiries.",
